# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored; this template is not.
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Never add a value to THIS file. It is committed, and a key pasted here is public the
# moment it is pushed. Values belong in .env.local only.

# Anthropic API key, used server-side by the draft-generation route handler and by the
# eval suite (`pnpm evals`).
#
# The key is read on the server only and is never exposed to the browser — note the
# absence of a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, which would inline it into the client bundle. Do
# not add one.
#
# Get one at: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
#
# USE A SEPARATE KEY FOR CI. The GitHub Actions secret (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, consumed by
# .github/workflows/evals.yml) should be a distinct credential from the one in your
# .env.local, not a copy of it. Two reasons: a key that leaks from a workflow log or a
# compromised action can be revoked without interrupting local work, and per-key usage
# in the console tells you whether spend came from CI or from a developer's machine.
# The eval suite bills real tokens, so that distinction is worth having.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
